<title>SINGAPORE: First Engineering net slumps 45 pct.</title>
<headline>First Engineering net slumps 45 pct.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-06-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to March 31, 1997</p>
<p>		   (in millions of S$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit			     1.21  vs   2.19</p>
<p>    Group shr (cents)		    1.70  vs   3.09</p>
<p>    Turnover				73.51  vs  48.67</p>
<p>    Other income incl. interest	0.24  vs   0.19</p>
<p>    Interest (expense)		   1.30  vs   0.88</p>
<p>    Depreciation (expense)	     3.58  vs   2.91</p>
<p>    Losses from associates	     0.13  vs   0.15</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit			 1.84  vs   2.80</p>
<p>    Tax					0.16  vs   0.39</p>
<p>    Minorities		   (loss)  0.34  vs   0.07 (loss)</p>
<p>Note - First Engineering Ltd said profits were hit by higher operating costs and difficult trading conditions in the electronics sector.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703011)</p>
</text>
